      "writtenOn": "2020-01-10T19:44:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We may run into a problem due to there being different ports. Say I enable ports 0 and 1, later I one of the ports, SPE will now be off even though 1 of the ports is still active. Before that didn\u0027t really matter since SPE was enabled and disabled each call.\n\nI\u0027d expect spi_master_shutdown to at least disable the dma_disable() since that\u0027s clearly specific to a port. But I\u0027m not so certain about the spi_clear_rx_fifo(spi) along with the calls to disable parts in CR1 and CR2.\n\nShould those other calls be conditioned on all(spi_enabled) \u003d\u003d 0?",
      "revId": "bf3e489730ab891605cbd290f1aeb29e0e234c16",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c6b53fde_5252b170",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/spi_master.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 257,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-13T21:26:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is ControlRegister1 and ControlRegister2 for each SPI port, so we are only turning on and off the SPE bit for a single SPI port at a time.\n\nThe clear fifo is also reading that ports SPI data as well.\n\nAs I read the code, it does appear that all of the code in shutdown is targeted towards a specific port.\n\nI appreciate you taking the time to think through this! Thanks for the review 😊",
      "parentUuid": "58148c87_bd0dd87e",
      "revId": "bf3e489730ab891605cbd290f1aeb29e0e234c16",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
